---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Chaos Knights Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Chaos Knights? Learn how they play, how to paint their corrupted armor, and exactly what to buy first as a walking engine of destruction."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">⛓️</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Chaos Knights</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Towering war machines corrupted by Chaos. Their noble pilot-lords fell to ambition, 
            desperation, and daemonic whispers — and their Knights warped around them. Now they 
            stalk the galaxy as Dread Households, engines of ruin bound to no master but ruin itself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Walking War Machines</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Hard</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$165+</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-3 italic">*No Combat Patrol box exists for Chaos Knights. Entry point is 3x War Dog Executioners — playable and competitive.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">The fallen houses</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          Imperial Knight households are ancient institutions — noble families bound to their 
          war machines across generations, each Knight bound to its pilot through a neural 
          interface called the Throne Mechanicum. For millennia they served the Imperium 
          faithfully. Then some did not.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some fell through ambition — a Knight lord who bargained with Chaos for greater power 
          and found the price was everything. Some fell through desperation — households that 
          swore themselves to a Chaos warband to survive a war the Imperium had abandoned them to. 
          Some fell through madness — the Throne Mechanicum is a psychically active device, 
          and in the wrong circumstances, it whispers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Whatever the cause, the result is the same. The Knight warps. Spines and blades grow 
          from the hull. Daemonic entities fuse with the machine-spirit. The pilot becomes 
          something else — still in there, still screaming, but no longer in control. These 
          are Chaos Knights: Dread Households that march under the banners of the Dark Gods, 
          bringing ruin to all they encounter.
        </p>
        <p>
          War Dogs are smaller Chaos equivalents of Imperial Armiger-class Knights — fast, 
          aggressive, and utterly unpredictable. They hunt in packs, serving the great 
          Chaos Knights as hounds serve hunters, except these hounds are the size of tanks.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Chaos Knights are a <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">super-heavy army</strong> — every 
          model is a massive war machine worth hundreds of points. A typical army has only 
          3–6 models total. You are not managing squads. You are managing engines of destruction.
        </p>
        <p>
          Compared to Imperial Knights, Chaos Knights skew aggressively toward melee. 
          War Dogs are fast and excellent at getting into combat quickly. Full-sized Chaos 
          Knights — Desecrators, Tyrants, and Abominants — hit harder in close combat than 
          their Imperial equivalents and can receive Daemonic Corruption upgrades that push 
          their capabilities further in exchange for instability.
        </p>
        <p>
          The appeal: few models means low cognitive overhead. You will never be overwhelmed 
          by bookkeeping thirty units. Each activation matters enormously — your Knights are 
          individually powerful enough to swing the whole game. Devastating when piloted well, 
          manageable to learn on.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Chaos Knights are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You love giant corrupted war machines</li>
            <li>✓ You want a small model count army (3–6 models)</li>
            <li>✓ You prefer melee-focused aggression</li>
            <li>✓ You want a high visual impact on the table</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy painting large centrepiece models</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want lots of models on the table</li>
            <li>✗ You hate painting large flat panels</li>
            <li>✗ You want a beginner-friendly entry price</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer ranged, shooty armies</li>
            <li>✗ You need a Combat Patrol box to start small</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Dread Hierarchy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">The Knight classes</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Chaos Knights come in two size categories. Your army will be built from these choices.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        {[
          {
            name: 'War Dog Executioner',
            size: 'Armiger-class (small)',
            role: 'Fast melee harasser',
            desc: 'The recommended starting purchase. Three War Dogs form a legal and highly competitive patrol. Armed with twin diabolus heavy stubbers and a slaughterclaw. Fast enough to threaten flanks on turn one.',
          },
          {
            name: 'War Dog Karnivore',
            size: 'Armiger-class (small)',
            role: 'Pure melee hunter',
            desc: 'The most melee-focused War Dog. Reaper chaintalon for devastating close combat. Less shooting than the Executioner but hits harder up close. A pack of these is terrifying.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Chaos Knight Desecrator',
            size: 'Knight-class (full size)',
            role: 'Melee centrepiece',
            desc: 'The full-sized Chaos Knight most players start with. Immense melee output via the laser destructor and titanic feet. The centerpiece of any Dread Household.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Chaos Knight Tyrant',
            size: 'Knight-class (full size)',
            role: 'Ranged fire support',
            desc: 'A full Knight skewed toward shooting. The Warpstrike cannon is devastating at range. A good complement to War Dogs doing the aggressive flanking work.',
          },
          {
            name: 'Chaos Knight Abominant',
            size: 'Knight-class (full size)',
            role: 'Melee monster',
            desc: 'The most corrupted and daemonically enhanced full Knight. Devastating in combat, radiates Chaos corruption onto nearby units. The apex predator of the Dread Household.',
          },
        ].map(knight => (
          <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
              <div class="flex-1">
                <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-3 mb-1">
                  <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg">{knight.name}</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">{knight.size}</span>
                  <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-[#c9a84c]">{knight.role}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">{knight.desc}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-6 italic">
        War Dogs and full Knights from the same kit build multiple configurations — 
        check the sprue options before buying multiples to maximise flexibility.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Chaos Knights</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Large panels + corruption effects = a challenging but spectacular result. 
        The key is building up the corruption gradually rather than trying to do it all at once.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Prime black, base coat your armor color</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Chaos Black spray primer. Then base coat the armor panels in your chosen Household color — Iron Warriors go Leadbelcher, others might use dark red (Khorne Red) or rotted metal. Pick one identity and commit.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Wash the whole model with Nuln Oil</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Apply Nuln Oil (or Agrax Earthshade for warmer tones) across all panels. Work into the recesses, cracks, and joint areas heavily. This is your shadow layer and rust foundation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush the armor panels</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Drybrush raised edges with a lighter version of your armor color. For metallics: Ironbreaker over Leadbelcher. This restores color to the high points and creates wear lines automatically.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Sponge on rust and chipping</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Tear a small piece of blister foam, dab it in Rhinox Hide, and lightly stipple along edges and lower panels. Then do the same with Skrag Brown. This is the fastest corruption effect and looks immediately convincing.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Daemonic energy in the cracks</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Pick a Chaos power color: sickly green (Tesseract Glow), purple (Magos Purple), or orange-red (Bloodletter). Apply as a Contrast paint or glaze into panel gaps, eye lenses, and corruption vents. This is the defining visual of Chaos Knights.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Pick out the bone and metal details</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Spines and bone growths: Ushabti Bone base → Agrax Earthshade → Screaming Skull drybrush. Metallic trim: Balthasar Gold washed with Agrax. The base: Stirland Mud texture paint, dried and drybrushed Karak Stone.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The corruption shortcut</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Prime black → spray <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Leadbelcher</strong> from above only → 
          apply <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Nuln Oil Gloss</strong> everywhere → 
          drybrush <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Ironbreaker</strong> on panels → 
          apply <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Plaguebearer Flesh Contrast</strong> or 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Tesseract Glow</strong> into cracks → 
          done. Three hours, table-ready result, unmistakably Chaos.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">There's no Combat Patrol for Chaos Knights. Start with three War Dogs — they form a legal patrol and are genuinely competitive.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$128</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">3x War Dog Executioners</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Three boxes gives you a small but legal Chaos Knights army. War Dogs are 
          fast, hit hard in melee, and each one is an imposing centrepiece model. 
          Paint all three before buying anything else — large models take time.
          Each kit also builds the Karnivore variant, so look at the weapons and pick 
          what suits your planned playstyle.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=chaos+knights+war+dog+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160 · centrepiece expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Chaos Knight (Desecrator / Tyrant / Abominant)</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Once your War Dogs are painted, add a full Chaos Knight as your army's anchor. 
          One box builds the Desecrator, Tyrant, or Abominant — decide which role you 
          want before assembling, as the builds are meaningfully different in how they play.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=chaos+knight+desecrator+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Chaos Black Spray', use: 'Primer — the foundation for everything', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'Metallic armor base coat', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil Gloss', use: 'Deep shadow in all recesses', required: true },
            { name: 'Ironbreaker', use: 'Drybrush highlight on armor panels', required: true },
            { name: 'Rhinox Hide + Skrag Brown', use: 'Rust and chipping via sponge', required: true },
            { name: 'Tesseract Glow or Plaguebearer Flesh', use: 'Daemonic energy in cracks and vents', required: true },
            { name: 'Ushabti Bone + Screaming Skull', use: 'Bone growths and spines', required: false },
            { name: 'Balthasar Gold', use: 'Metallic trim and heraldry details', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: '3x War Dog Executioners', cost: '~$128', note: 'Minimum legal army — three impressive models' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (8)', cost: '~$45', note: 'Metallics, rust effects, daemonic glow' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tufts + grey drybrush' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Plastic glue', cost: '~$7', note: 'Large kits need plastic glue, not super glue' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">Starter total (War Dogs only)</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$212</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Adding a full Chaos Knight (~$160) brings the total to ~$372 for a fuller list. 
        Unlike most factions, three War Dogs is already a genuinely playable army — 
        you don't need the big Knight immediately.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">The household falls. The hunt begins.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Three War Dogs. Three towering engines of Chaos. 
        Paint them before buying anything else — they reward patience and attention.
        The corruption paints itself once you start.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
